  "evidence": "TEXT_E: Brexit implemented and new FTAs; Union focus with retention of First Past the Post and voter ID; Defence: exceed NATO 2%, maintain nuclear deterrent, modernise forces; Policing and justice: 20,000 more police, tougher sentences, more prison places; Immigration: Australian‑style points system, stronger enforcement; NHS and social care: record funding uplift, care cost guarantee; Economy: no rises in main taxes, National Living Wage linked to median earnings. TEXT_G: Scottish independence referendum; closest possible EU relationship and potential revoke of Article 50; Defence: cancel UK nuclear weapons system; Democracy: replace FPTP with STV, abolish unelected second chamber, extend voting to 16–17‑year‑olds and all lawful residents; Care/equality measures: NHS Protection Act, end benefit freeze and sanctions, uprate benefits, supervised drug consumption facilities, allow asylum seekers to work and expand family reunion.",
  "reasoning": "Given Loyalty is the top priority, along with notable weight on Authority and some on Proportionality, TEXT_E aligns better through strong unionism, defence/nuclear deterrence, policing and controlled immigration, while still offering Care via NHS and social care. TEXT_G scores higher on Care and Equality but conflicts with the profile’s Loyalty emphasis (independence drive, scrapping nuclear) and shows weaker Authority/Proportionality cues, making TEXT_E the closer fit overall.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_E"
}
